# Stanimir, elder of the Tser Pool camp (docs/voice/stanimir.md). He greets the party as they come into the camp
# (approach), sells camp goods (shop), tells the old story, and takes the news of his nephew Nicu, the hanged man at
# the crossroads (crossroads.dialogue). Robbing his strongbox (tser_pool container) turns him; refusing to give it back
# starts the camp brawl (tser_pool_brawl).

~ start
if flag.vistani_turned_hostile
-> hostile
endif
if flag.vistani_robbed and not flag.vistani_repaid and not flag.stanimir_deceived
-> confront
endif
if flag.tser_pool_arrived
-> again
endif
set tser_pool_arrived
if not flag.eva_met
quest madam_evas_reading invited
endif
Narrator: A huge grey-bearded man in a red sash rises from beside the fire with a fiddle in one hand and a cup in the other, and spreads both arms as if you were family come home late.
Stanimir [smile]: Guests! Off the road, out of the dark, into the light! I am Stanimir. The fire is free, the wine is cheap, and the music is the best in Barovia, because it is the only music in Barovia.
if guest:ireena
Stanimir: And you bring the burgomaster's girl, out past the crossroads. Well, well. Sit near the fire, lady. Not too near the trees.
Ireena: You knew my father?
Stanimir: Everyone knew your father. He shouted at me for an hour once, about a horse. Best conversation I had that year.
endif
if flag.crossroads_gallows_seen
Narrator: His eyes go to your faces, one by one, and stop. Whatever the road has written on them, he reads part of it.
endif
Stanimir: Madam Eva is in the big tent. She has been expecting you. Don't ask me how; I stopped asking forty years ago.
-> menu

~ again
if flag.eva_threatened and not flag.eva_reading_done
Stanimir [angry]: You showed the old woman your teeth in her own tent. I play the fiddle at my fire, friends; I don't play the fool. Mind your manners in that tent.
endif
if flag.nicu_kin_told
Stanimir [sad]: Sit, friends. Sit. The fire is still free, and for you the wine is too.
else
Stanimir [smile]: Back at my fire! Good. Sit, drink, tell me lies about the road.
endif
-> menu

~ menu
* [if flag.crossroads_gallows_seen and not flag.nicu_kin_told] We found a young Vistana hanged at the crossroads. -> nicu_news
* [if not flag.stanimir_wine_shared] Share a cup of your wine. -> wine
* Show us what you have to trade. -> trade
* Tell us about Madam Eva. -> about_eva
* [if not flag.stanimir_tale_heard] Tell us a story. -> tale
* [name:ilse_varga] [if flag.kestrel_tally_tser and not flag.kestrel_jory_told] Ask about the soldiers your people guided a year ago. -> companions/kestrel:stanimir
* [if not flag.stanimir_read] [Insight DC 14] Who do your people answer to? -> answer_ok | answer_fail
* Goodbye. -> END

~ nicu_news
Narrator: The fiddle goes down on the log beside him, very carefully, as if it might break.
Stanimir: Silver earring shaped like a horse's head? Black hair, too long? A laugh like a donkey falling downstairs?
* [if flag.nicu_token_taken] Put the earring in his hand. -> nicu_earring
* Tell him what you saw. -> nicu_told

~ nicu_earring
Narrator: His hand closes over the earring and stays closed.
-> nicu_told

~ nicu_told
set nicu_kin_told
quest the_hanged_vistana told
attitude stanimir friendly
Stanimir [sad]: Nicu. My sister's boy. He rode to Vallaki to sell a horse, and he came home by the crossroads after all.
if flag.nicu_cut_down
Stanimir: You cut him down. Strangers, and you stopped and cut him down, when nobody else on that road would slow their horse.
if flag.nicu_rites_said
Stanimir: With words said over him, even. I don't know your gods. I hope they knew him.
endif
elif flag.crossroads_dead_cleared
Stanimir [angry]: He walked again? This land won't even let our dead lie down. Then you gave him his rest the hard way. That is still a gift.
else
Stanimir: Still hanging, then. I'll go myself, tonight, with a knife and a good horse, and bring him home.
endif
Stanimir: Luminita must hear it from me. Not from you. From me.
Stanimir: And listen. Somebody in this camp will send word up the hill that you passed this way. That is how it is with us. It will be me, and I will tell him you went east. Small thing. Big thing. Both.
set stanimir_misdirects
interject tag:veteran: That's a real favour. We won't forget it.
-> menu

~ wine
set stanimir_wine_shared
Stanimir [smile]: Plum wine, from plums that grew in a summer before any of you were born. Drink! It won't hurt. Much.
Narrator: It goes down like warm honey and lands like a kick. For a moment the valley feels almost like somewhere people live on purpose.
interject species:dwarf: Strong. Too sweet. I'll need a second cup to be certain.
interject species:halfling: I'd like the recipe. I'd like the recipe very much.
-> menu

~ trade
Stanimir: Rope, oil, food that keeps, blankets that keep you. Two potions, very dear, because they are very dear to me.
shop
Stanimir: A pleasure! Come again. Bring more gold and less mud.
-> menu

~ about_eva
Stanimir: Madam Eva has been old since my grandmother was a girl. She reads the cards for whoever the road brings, and the road brings whoever the cards want.
Stanimir: Pay her what she asks. It is never only money, and it is never more than you can spare. Usually.
-> menu

~ tale
set stanimir_tale_heard
Stanimir: Once there was a prince who won this valley with his sword, and he had a younger brother whom everybody loved. The brother was to marry a girl as lovely as a spring morning. The prince wanted her.
Stanimir: On the wedding day, the prince made a bargain with something under the world. He killed his brother. The bride ran from him, and the castle wall was high, and the gorge below it was very deep.
Stanimir: His own guards filled him with arrows. He did not die. He has been not dying ever since. Drink! It's a wedding story. It should end with a drink.
if guest:ireena
Ireena [afraid]: I know the end of that story. I've dreamed it. The wall, and the wind, and somebody calling a name that isn't mine.
Stanimir: Then we will play something cheerful. Something very loud and very cheerful.
endif
interject name:liriel_dawnsong: A bargain with something under the world. Then that is why the morning stays away.
-> menu

~ answer_ok
set stanimir_read
set vistani_spies_suspected
Narrator: His eyes go to the dark line of the hills above the trees, once, before his smile comes back.
Stanimir: We answer to the road and the cards. And a little, yes, to the man on the hill. He lets our wagons through the mist. A dog doesn't bite the hand that holds the gate.
-> menu

~ answer_fail
set stanimir_read
Stanimir [smile]: To the fire, the fiddle and Madam Eva, in that order on a good day. On a bad day, to my wife.
-> menu

~ confront
Narrator: Stanimir is not smiling. Two younger Vistani stand behind him with their thumbs hooked in their belts, close to their knives.
Stanimir [angry]: My strongbox is lighter by forty gold, and you are the only strangers in my camp. I will ask once.
* Give it back. -> repay
* [Deception DC 16] We never touched it. -> lie_ok | lie_fail
* It's ours now. Come and take it. -> fight

~ repay
gold -40
set vistani_repaid
Stanimir: Good. A guest who takes and then gives back is still a guest. Barely. Sit, but sit where I can see your hands.
interject name:kip_smudgewick: We're very sorry. Truly. Have an apricot as well. No obligation.
-> menu

~ lie_ok
set stanimir_deceived
Narrator: He looks at you for a long moment, and then at the two young men behind him, and you can see him deciding which of them to shout at later.
Stanimir: Then one of my own owes me an apology. Sit. I'm sorry I asked.
interject class:cleric: We'll put it right before we leave. Won't we.
-> menu

~ lie_fail
Stanimir [angry]: You lie the way I play the flute: loudly and badly. Give it back. And ten more, for making me listen to it.
* [if gold >= 50] Give it back, and the ten. (50 gp) -> repay_liar
* [if not (gold >= 50)] Give back the forty. It's all we have. -> repay_short
* Come and take it. -> fight

~ repay_liar
gold -50
set vistani_repaid
Stanimir: Forty for the box, ten for the flute solo. Sit, but sit where I can see your hands. And nobody sings.
-> menu

~ repay_short
gold -40
set vistani_repaid
attitude stanimir indifferent
Stanimir: Forty. You owe me ten and a true word, and I will never see either. Sit if you must. The wine is not free tonight.
-> menu

~ fight
Stanimir: As you like. Nobody robs my fire twice.
combat tser_pool_brawl

~ hostile
Stanimir [angry]: You put a knife to the old woman's throat in my camp. Walk through, if you must. Don't stop, and don't sit.
-> END
